### 1) Executive summary

  This spec recommends evolving markdown-preview into a Custom Text Editor–based preview-first editor (Option A): Markdown opens in a custom preview
  surface by default, and lightweight toolbar actions (Bold, Italic, Insert Code Block) edit the underlying TextDocument safely through extension-host
  edits. This aligns with VS Code’s intended model for editable custom views: CustomTextEditorProvider with the text document as source of truth,
  message-based UI events, and native undo/redo integration for text-backed edits (Custom Editors guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-
  guides/custom-editors)).

  The current repo already solves preview-first routing and mode orchestration, but it relies on built-in markdown preview commands and text-editor-
  only formatting, so it cannot provide true preview-surface editing. The proposed architecture reuses the project’s strong config/state/testing
  foundation, replaces preview rendering ownership with a custom editor webview, and introduces deterministic text transformation rules and message
  protocol contracts.

