  ### 3) Research findings (grouped by topic, each with citations)

  #### A) Webview security model (CSP, resources, messaging, sanitization)

  - VS Code webviews require explicit local resource conversion (asWebviewUri) and localResourceRoots scoping; this is a core security boundary
    (Webview guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/webview)).
  - VS Code explicitly recommends a strict CSP and minimizing capabilities; scripts should be enabled only when required (Webview guide (https://
    code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/webview)).
  - VS Code guidance explicitly calls out sanitizing all user/file-derived input and avoiding unsanitized injection into HTML (Webview guide (https://
    code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/webview)).
  - Message passing is the standard bridge (webview.postMessage / onDidReceiveMessage) (Webview guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-
    guides/webview)).
  - VS Code maintainers also pushed ecosystem-wide CSP adoption for webviews (warning effort) (Issue #79248 (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/
    issues/79248)).

  #### B) Custom Editor API: when/why, read/write, default behavior

  - Custom editors are intended for file-specific UX in editor area; text-backed custom editors should use CustomTextEditorProvider (Custom Editors
    guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/custom-editors)).
  - For custom text editors, TextDocument remains source of truth and VS Code handles text undo/redo semantics (Custom Editors guide (https://
    code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/custom-editors)).
  - Contribution point contributes.customEditors supports priority = default or option; default is used when no explicit user association exists
    (Contribution points (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/references/contribution-points#contributes.customEditors)).
  - Users can still override via workbench.editorAssociations (Contribution points (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/references/contribution-
    points#contributes.customEditors)).

  #### C) Built-in Markdown preview architecture and extension points

  - VS Code itself cites built-in Markdown preview as a webview example (Webview guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/webview)).
  - Markdown extension points support adding preview scripts/styles and markdown-it plugins (markdown.previewScripts, markdown.previewStyles,
    markdown.markdownItPlugins) (Markdown extension guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/markdown-extension)).
  - Built-in markdown extension contributes both command-based preview and a markdown preview custom editor (vscode.markdown.preview.editor, priority:
    option) (VS Code source package.json (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bfe8da141e578a3ef4b27848da16e561ea4ad8cd/extensions/markdown-
    language-features/package.json)).
  - Built-in renderer uses markdown-it/highlight pipeline and maintains a typed message protocol and debounced update path in preview manager code
    (markdownEngine.ts (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bfe8da141e578a3ef4b27848da16e561ea4ad8cd/extensions/markdown-language-features/src/
    markdownEngine.ts), preview.ts (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bfe8da141e578a3ef4b27848da16e561ea4ad8cd/extensions/markdown-language-
    features/src/preview/preview.ts), previewMessaging.d.ts (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bfe8da141e578a3ef4b27848da16e561ea4ad8cd/
    extensions/markdown-language-features/types/previewMessaging.d.ts)).

  #### D) UX and accessibility expectations for webviews

  - VS Code UX guidance says webviews are for cases native APIs cannot cover, and extensions should use native affordances where possible (Webview UX
    guidelines (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/ux-guidelines/webviews)).
  - Accessibility docs require predictable focus movement, including entering/leaving webviews (notably F6 flow) and clear keyboard navigation patterns
    (VS Code accessibility docs (https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/configure/accessibility/accessibility)).
  - Webviews should react to VS Code accessibility state (vscode-using-screen-reader, reduced motion) and theme tokens/classes (Webview guide (https://
    code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/webview)).

  #### E) Real-world implementation patterns (samples/extensions)

  - Official custom-editor sample pattern:
      - Text document as model.
      - onDidChangeTextDocument -> webview update.
      - webview -> extension message commands.
      - edits applied via WorkspaceEdit.
      - strict CSP + nonce in HTML template.
        (catScratchEditor sample (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-extension-samples/blob/61fda64ede073136f3716f69b067d212ef0893e1/custom-editor-
        sample/src/catScratchEditor.ts)).
  - Official webview sample pattern:
      - localResourceRoots, CSP+nonce, serializer rehydration, message wiring.
        (webview sample (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-extension-samples/blob/61fda64ede073136f3716f69b067d212ef0893e1/webview-sample/src/
        extension.ts)).
  - Reputable production extension pattern:
      - Draw.io uses custom editors with priority: default for file patterns, demonstrating default custom-editor ownership in practice.
        (vscode-drawio package.json (https://github.com/hediet/vscode-drawio/blob/21c8a129044a9fa99bd67bff16d1f36255ab6e73/package.json)).

  #### F) Community feedback on WYSIWYG/preview tradeoffs

  - VS Code maintainer feedback explicitly notes full Typora-style WYSIWYG is not core priority and several requested scenarios were not feasible with
    then-existing APIs; direction moved toward custom editor preview instead (Issue #2766 maintainer comment (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/
    issues/2766#issuecomment-375829223), Issue #84520 (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/84520)).
  - VS Code markdown custom editor rollout discussion shows practical stabilization needs: link behavior, scroll state, toggle flow, find widget,
    editor switching (Issue #84520 (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/84520), comment (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/
    issues/84520#issuecomment-740762825), comment (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/84520#issuecomment-555770873)).
  - Using preview editor as default has known workflow friction in diff/file-create contexts (high-signal user reports) (Issue #191565 (https://
    github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/191565), Issue #188338 (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/188338), analysis comment (https://
    github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/188338#issuecomment-2267098129)).
  - Extension maintainers in markdown ecosystem report many preview-pane behaviors are not feasible to implement from outside built-in markdown preview
    ownership (vscode-markdown issue #370 (https://github.com/yzhang-gh/vscode-markdown/issues/370), owner comment (https://github.com/yzhang-gh/
    vscode-markdown/issues/370#issuecomment-462250637)).

