  ### 5) Chosen architecture deep dive (detailed design)

  #### 5.1 User experience

  - Markdown files must open into markdownPreview.editor (custom text editor view) by default for normal file-open flows.
  - Toolbar actions must exist in editor title (Bold, Italic, Insert Code Block) and may be mirrored inside webview header.
  - Preview selection behavior:
      - Click in preview sets an anchor line.
      - Drag selection in preview resolves to line-span selection (deterministic, not pixel-perfect WYSIWYG).
      - If no resolvable selection exists, actions insert placeholders at anchor/cursor.
  - Keyboard:
      - Cmd/Ctrl+B => bold toggle.
      - Cmd/Ctrl+I => italic toggle.
      - `Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+`` => insert code block.
  - Focus:
      - F6 and Tab order must support entering/leaving webview predictably, matching VS Code accessibility model (Accessibility docs (https://
        code.visualstudio.com/docs/configure/accessibility/accessibility)).

  #### 5.2 Data model and synchronization

  - Source of truth must be the backing TextDocument from CustomTextEditorProvider (Custom Editors guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-
    guides/custom-editors)).
  - Sync loop:
      - onDidChangeTextDocument -> debounce 120–200ms -> send render update to all panels for same URI.
      - onDidReceiveMessage from webview -> validate payload -> compute text edit -> apply.
  - Edit apply path:
      - Use WorkspaceEdit/text-document edits from extension host.
      - Do not mutate DOM as source of truth.
  - Concurrency:
      - Every toolbar message includes documentVersion.
      - If stale, extension recalculates with current doc and line-anchor fallback; if unsafe, reject action and ask user to retry.
  - Undo/redo:
      - Must use text-document edit path so VS Code undo stack remains authoritative for text custom editor behavior (Custom Editors guide (https://
        code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/custom-editors)).
  - External file changes:
      - Must refresh render when disk/content changes are observed through text-document change events.

  #### 5.3 Editing operations (algorithms)

  - Bold toggle (**):
      - Non-empty selection:
          - If exactly wrapped by **...**, unwrap.
          - Else wrap with **.
      - Empty selection:
          - If cursor inside word, apply toggle to word.
          - Else insert **bold text** and select bold text.
  - Italic toggle (* preferred):
      - Non-empty selection:
          - If wrapped by *...* (not **...** only), unwrap.
          - Else wrap with *.
      - Empty selection:
          - Word-under-cursor toggle; else insert *italic text*.
      - In bold conflict case (**text**), italic wrap becomes ***text***; unitalic removes only one * layer.
  - Insert code block:
      - Empty selection:
          - Insert:

            ```lang
            code

          - Cursor selects code.
      - Non-empty selection:
          - Wrap selection in fenced block.
      - Indentation:
          - Preserve current line leading whitespace for both fences and body.
      - Multi-line selections: preserve content exactly; no normalization beyond fence insertion.
  - Edge-case policy:
      - When parser-safe toggle cannot be inferred (crossing partial markup boundaries), operation must fallback to wrap (non-destructive) rather than
        attempt risky unwrap.

  #### 5.4 Rendering pipeline

  - Parser:
      - Use markdown-it in webview runtime, with line-mapping plugin (data-line) similar to VS Code approach in principle (markdownEngine.ts (https://
        github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bfe8da141e578a3ef4b27848da16e561ea4ad8cd/extensions/markdown-language-features/src/markdownEngine.ts)).
  - Syntax highlighting:
      - Use highlight.js in markdown-it highlight callback for fenced blocks (same general pattern as built-in markdown renderer codebase)
        (markdownEngine.ts (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bfe8da141e578a3ef4b27848da16e561ea4ad8cd/extensions/markdown-language-features/
        src/markdownEngine.ts)).
      - Theme match should rely on VS Code CSS vars/classes in webview.
  - Security:
      - CSP with nonce, no inline scripts, strict default-src 'none', scoped img-src, style-src, script-src.
      - localResourceRoots must be minimal.
      - Sanitization must run before HTML insertion.
      - Message payloads must be schema-validated.
        (Webview guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/webview)).

  #### 5.5 UI implementation plan

  - Webview toolbar:
      - Buttons: Bold, Italic, Code Block.
      - ARIA labels and visible keyboard hints.
      - Theme via --vscode-* CSS vars and high-contrast class support.
  - Editor title actions:
      - Mirror same commands via menus.editor/title with when: activeCustomEditorId == markdownPreview.editor.
  - Accessibility:
      - Focus order must be deterministic.
      - Esc should return focus to editor group when toolbar focused.
      - Reduced-motion and screen-reader classes must be honored (Webview guide (https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/webview),
        Accessibility docs (https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/configure/accessibility/accessibility)).

  #### 5.6 Extension contributions

  - contributes.customEditors:
      - viewType: markdownPreview.editor
      - selector: *.md, *.markdown
      - priority: default or staged option + explicit association policy.
  - Commands:
      - markdownPreview.toggleBold
      - markdownPreview.toggleItalic
      - markdownPreview.insertCodeBlock
      - markdownPreview.openSource (safety escape hatch)
  - Menus:
      - editor/title buttons active only for custom editor.
  - Keybindings:
      - Bind above commands for custom-editor context.
  - Configuration:
      - markdownPreview.previewFirst.enabled
      - markdownPreview.render.debounceMs
      - markdownPreview.security.allowRemoteImages
      - markdownPreview.selection.mode (lineSpan default, future smartText).

  #### 5.7 Code structure and beginner-friendly standards

  - Keep:
      - src/services/config-service.ts
      - src/services/logger.ts
      - src/services/validation-service.ts
      - i18n utility.
  - Refactor:
      - src/services/preview-service.ts to become custom-editor orchestration (or replace with provider-focused service).
      - src/handlers/markdown-file-handler.ts to call vscode.openWith for custom view (normal opens only).
      - src/services/formatting-service.ts into pure transform engine + apply layer.
  - Add:
      - src/editors/markdownPreviewEditorProvider.ts
      - src/editors/markdownDocumentSync.ts
      - src/editing/markdownTransforms.ts
      - src/webview/previewEditor/index.html
      - src/webview/previewEditor/main.ts
      - src/webview/protocol.ts
  - Dependency policy:
      - Must keep minimal (markdown-it, highlight.js, sanitizer).
      - Every dependency should have one clear reason.
  - Error handling:
      - Centralized logger + user-facing toast for rejected edits.
      - Recover safely on stale-version actions.

